    "scope": "15.e.W/R native Linux journaled extraction of currently verifiable project and partial bundles. Existing BootstrapTree owns no-replace publication, configuration-last ordering, rollback and retained proof. Complete projects reopen and remain subject to normal write gates. Partials are conservatively excluded from the complete-project reader until 15.f; no context promotion or implicit rehydration. No cross-platform, unimplemented portable receipts, authenticity, full semantic validation or release claim. R guards the original input and exact root namespace at every publication boundary and after receipt retention. Interrupted replay retains its proven prefix and never reports success after a fault; fresh ordinary failures restore the owned original state or retain the complete published root. Unverifiable/foreign remnants are retained as conflicts. 18.v binds the replacement interruption/normal-completion oracles; old automatic-repair evidence is historical only. Further plan scopes and release acceptance remain separate."
  },
